    {
      "title": "Indian national missing after attacks on commercial vessel in Hormuz",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/indian-national-missing-after-attacks-on-commercial-vessel-in-hormuz-126111800012_1.html",
      "description": "An Indian national went missing and two others sustained injuries after their Panama-flagged vessel came under attack in the Strait of Hormuz this week that triggered a strong condemnation from New Delhi.\nThe Ministry of External Affairs (MEA) said of the 24 Indian nationals on board MT Tara Gas, 21 have been safely evacuated.\n\"We condemn the attack on the Panama-flagged LPG tanker MT Tara Gas in the Strait of Hormuz on 16 November 16,\" it said in a statement.\nIndia said the targeting of commercial shipping and civilian infrastructure must end.\n\"Of the 24 Indian nationals on board, 21 have been safely evacuated ashore at Khasab, two injured Indian crew members have been admitted to hospital, while one Indian national remains missing,\" it added.\nThe MEA said the Embassy in Oman is closely monitoring the ongoing search and rescue operations in coordination with the Omani authorities.\n\"We appreciate the timely assistance and support extended by the Government of Oman in the rescue .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-18T02:15:08"
    }
